system "ISO:new-Newa:Latn:15919-2026" {

metadata {
  authority_id iso
  id 15919-2026
  language iso-639-2:new
  source_script Newa
  destination_script Latn
  name "ISO/DIS 15919 (2026) Information and documentation -- Transliteration of Indic scripts into Latin characters (Newar (Newa); DIS stage)"
  url https://www.iso.org/committee/48820.html
  creation_date 2026
  adoption_date 2026
  description {    Second edition (DIS stage) of ISO 15919, Transliteration of Indic scripts into Latin characters.
    Encoded from the committee ballot ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N125; per-script tables of clause 7,
    numerals of normative Annex A, Rule 17 Vedic accents, and options 9.8/9.9/9.10 as
    selectable variants (languages opt98 opt99 opt10). See notes for provenance and errata.  }

  notes {
    note "Encoded from ISO/DIS 15919 (2026), ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N125 (DIS stage draft, 2026-01-26), Table 7.17 plus the numerals of normative Annex A Table A.2; shared-table content verified against ISO/CD 15919 (2025, N108) and ISO 15919 WD (2024, N88). The DIS is not yet a published International Standard."
    note "Rule 2 convention: inherent a with a consonant is always transliterated (consonant rows carry the inherent a)."
    note "virama is deleted in the default behavior (clause 6 printed virama hex list); option 9.10 (language selector opt10) instead renders virama as middle dot U+00B7."
    note "Option selectors (W3 languages, single-select): opt98 = clause 9.8 upper-case for all initial vowels (first letter capitalised for digraph outputs); opt99 = clause 9.9 unusual conjuncts marked with equals sign U+003D via the script's zero-width joiner; opt10 = clause 9.10 explicit virama middle dot. Option 9.1 (non-uniform e/o) is available by character substitution on outputs and is not separately staged."
    note "DIS errata recorded: Table 7.17 row NGHA 11413 prints Hex '1445 0324 0067' (leading typo) and row NYHA 11419 prints Hex '00F1 0324 0067' while both Latin text cells read n̤a (n + U+0324 + a); the Latin text is encoded. NGHA, NYHA and NHA 11424 all print n̤a (colliding outputs, as printed)."
    note "Row-level source errata encoded per printed text: Table 7.17 row ['𑐓']: latin/hex mismatch: text='n̤a' hex=1445 0324 0067 | Table 7.17 row ['𑐙']: latin/hex mismatch: text='n̤a' hex=00F1 0324 0067 | Table 7.17 row ['𑐯']: latin/hex mismatch: text='l̤a' hex=006C 0324"
    note "Row LLA 1142F is encoded l̤a (006C 0324 0061), matching the printed Latin cell's mark order like the other under-diaeresis rows."
  }
}

languages opt98 opt99 opt10

tests {
   "𑐀" ->  "a"
   "𑐎" ->  "ka"
   "𑐁" ->  "ā"
   "𑐵" ->  "ā"
